This extension adds Deus Ex: Mankind Divided modding support to Vortex Mod Manager.

[b]✅ Supported Versions:[/b]
[list]
[*]Steam[/*]
[*]GOG[/*]
[*]Epic[/*]
[*]Other versions may need to select the installation location manually.[/*]
[/list]
[b]🛠️ Mod Installation Notes:[/b]
[list]
[*]Root Folder mods with a "DLC" folder install to the game folder.[/*]
[*]Runtime file mods with a "Game.layer.0.all.archive", "Game.layer.0.en.archive", "Game.layer.1.all.archive", "Game.layer.1.en.archive", "Game.layer.0.de.archive", "Game.layer.1.de.archive" or one of 12 other named files install to the "runtime" folder.[/*]
[*]DLC runtime file mods with a "DLC01.layer.0.all.archive", "DLC02.layer.0.all.archive", "DLCPackAssault.layer.0.all.archive", "DLCPackClassic.layer.0.all.archive", "DLCPackEnforcer.layer.0.all.archive", "DLCPackIntruder.layer.0.all.archive", "DLCPackTactical.layer.0.all.archive" or "DLCPreOrder.layer.0.all.archive" file install to the "DLC\runtime" folder.[/*]
[*]Binaries (Engine Injector) mods with a ".dll", ".exe", ".asi" or ".addon64" file install to the "retail" folder.[/*]
[*]Archives with a FOMOD installer (a "fomod" folder with ModuleConfig.xml) are handed to Vortex's built-in FOMOD installer instead.[/*]
[/list]
[b]📋 Usage Notes:[/b]
[list]
[*]You can open several useful files/folders/URLs using the buttons within the folder icon on the Mods toolbar.[/*]
[/list]

[b]📝 Notes for Mod Authors:[/b]
[spoiler]
Packaging rules for Deus Ex: Mankind Divided mods, so Vortex installs them to the right place.

Vortex decides what a mod is by looking at the files and folders inside the archive. It tries each installer in order and the first one that matches wins, so archive layout is what determines where your mod ends up.

========================================================================

Root / Game Folder Mods:

For mods laid out the same way the files appear inside the game folder. Vortex copies the matched folder and everything under it straight into the game.

[code]
MyRootMod.zip
└── DLC\
    └── ... files in their real relative locations
[/code]

  Requirements:
    - Recognised by a folder named "DLC", "retail" or "runtime" in the archive.

  Installs to: the game folder

  Common mistakes:
    - Zipping the folder that CONTAINS the game folders, instead of the game folders themselves, adds an extra level and misplaces every file.

========================================================================

runtime file:

Recognised when the archive contains a "Game.layer.0.all.archive", "Game.layer.0.en.archive", "Game.layer.1.all.archive", "Game.layer.1.en.archive", "Game.layer.0.de.archive", "Game.layer.1.de.archive", "Game.layer.0.es.archive", "Game.layer.1.es.archive", "Game.layer.0.fr.archive", "Game.layer.1.fr.archive", "Game.layer.0.it.archive", "Game.layer.1.it.archive", "Game.layer.0.mx.archive", "Game.layer.1.mx.archive", "Game.layer.0.pt.archive", "Game.layer.1.pt.archive", "Game.layer.0.ru.archive" or "Game.layer.1.ru.archive" file.

  Installs to: "runtime"

========================================================================

DLC runtime file:

Recognised when the archive contains a "DLC01.layer.0.all.archive", "DLC02.layer.0.all.archive", "DLCPackAssault.layer.0.all.archive", "DLCPackClassic.layer.0.all.archive", "DLCPackEnforcer.layer.0.all.archive", "DLCPackIntruder.layer.0.all.archive", "DLCPackTactical.layer.0.all.archive" or "DLCPreOrder.layer.0.all.archive" file.

  Installs to: "DLC\runtime"

========================================================================

Binaries (Engine Injector):

Recognised when the archive contains a ".dll", ".exe", ".asi" or ".addon64" file.

  Installs to: "retail"

========================================================================

Rules That Apply To Every Mod Type:

    - Archives that contain a FOMOD installer (a "fomod" folder with "ModuleConfig.xml") are handed to Vortex's built-in FOMOD installer instead, and none of the rules above apply.
    - Folder and file name matching is case-insensitive.
    - Extra wrapper folders around a recognised folder are generally fine; the installer searches at any depth.
[/spoiler]

